/* WIDGET STAT BLOCKS — wrap at two per row instead of overflowing the card.
 *
 * homepage lays a widget's stat blocks out as a non-wrapping `flex-row` inside a card that
 * carries Tailwind's `overflow-clip`, so a row wider than the card is SILENTLY CUT OFF on the
 * right rather than wrapped or scrolled. Karakeep's four stats needed 335px in a 272px card:
 * 63px of "HIGHLIGHTS" simply vanished. Nothing reports this — no console error, no pod log,
 * and the tile keeps rendering.
 *
 * Two stats per row rather than three or a content-based fit, because it also EQUALISES TILE
 * HEIGHT, which three does not. Every widget here carries two, three or four stats, so at two
 * per row they all occupy exactly two stat rows and every widgeted tile lands on the same
 * height. Measured 2026-09-09 at 1920px: 13 widgeted tiles, all 172px, against 120px/136px
 * before. `.services-list` is a CSS grid, so tiles already stretch to their row's tallest
 * member — making the content uniform is what makes the stretch invisible.
 *
 * `overflow-wrap: anywhere` is the backstop for a narrow viewport. At 1280px a single long
 * label ("BOOKMARKS") still overran its half-width block by 7px, and a one-word label has no
 * break opportunity of its own. It engages only when a label genuinely does not fit, so it
 * changes nothing at 1920px.
 *
 * The `w-10` rule is the coinmarketcap widget's percent-change column: a fixed 2.5rem against
 * "-0.46%", which needs 43px. Negative values with two decimals clipped by 3px.
 *
 * #my-calendar is excluded throughout — it is a single full-width child laid out as a column
 * by the rules below, and a 50% flex-basis has no business there.
 *
 * VERIFY BY MEASURING, not by looking: `scrollWidth > clientWidth` on every descendant of
 * `li.service` finds a clipped block; the tile's own `<li>` does NOT show it, because the
 * clipping happens on the `div.service-card` inside it. Checking the `<li>` is what let this
 * ship in the first place.
 */
li.service:not(#my-calendar) .service-container {
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}

li.service:not(#my-calendar) .service-container > div {
  /* NO GROW — the `0` in the first position is the whole point. With `flex-grow: 1` an odd
   * stat count left the last block stretched across the full row: the five three-stat widgets
   * rendered 128px, 128px, then a 264px block, against a uniform 128px on the four-stat ones.
   * Same tile height, visibly different blocks. Growth disabled, every block is 128px and an
   * odd count simply leaves the last half-row empty, which reads as a grid rather than as a
   * mistake. Measured 2026-09-09 at 1920px across all nine Services tiles. */
  flex: 0 0 calc(50% - 0.5rem);
  min-width: 0;
}

li.service:not(#my-calendar) .service-container > div > div {
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

li.service:not(#my-calendar) .service-container .font-bold.w-10 {
  width: auto;
  min-width: 3.25rem;
}

#my-calendar .service-container > div {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  max-height: 427px;
  overflow: hidden;
}

/* Target the events list directly - it's the last div inside the calendar content */
#my-calendar .service-container > div > div:last-child {
  overflow-y: auto;
  min-height: 0;
}

#my-calendar .service-container > div > div:last-child::-webkit-scrollbar {
  width: 4px;
}
#my-calendar .service-container > div > div:last-child::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
  background: transparent;
}
#my-calendar .service-container > div > div:last-child::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
  border-radius: 2px;
}
